course: dictionary
lesson: 10860
title: Vibrato, the warm wobble
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vibrato is a quick, small wobble up and down in the pitch of a note. Pitch means how high or low a note sounds. Singers and players of violin, cello or flute can make vibrato to make the sound warmer and richer.
explain: Read the context: «Vibrato is a controlled wobble in the voice that singers use on purpose, different from a nervous shake.» The clues are «controlled» and «on purpose». A nervous shake happens by accident. Vibrato is chosen by the singer.
explain: Music teachers say vibrato makes a note sound alive and expressive. You can sing with vibrato, or use a wide vibrato, which wobbles more, or too much vibrato, which can sound messy. Listen to a violin and hear whether the note wobbles gently.
explain: In science, vibrato links to sound and vibration. Sound is made when things vibrate, and pitch depends on how fast they vibrate. So a wobble in pitch is a wobble in those vibrations.
fact: Vibrato means a quick, small wobble in the pitch of a note.
fact: «Vibrato» is made on purpose by a singer or by a player of a string or wind instrument.
fact: Vibrato makes the sound warmer and richer.
fact: Phrases you may hear: «sing with vibrato», «a wide vibrato», «too much vibrato».
fact: In science, pitch depends on how fast something vibrates.
exercise: What is vibrato? | A type of musical instrument | A long pause between songs | *A quick, small wobble up and down in the pitch of a note | A loud drum beat
exercise: The text says vibrato is «different from a nervous shake». What is the difference? | A nervous shake makes music richer | They are exactly the same | Vibrato is a kind of cold | *Vibrato is done on purpose; a nervous shake happens by accident
exercise: Which phrase describes a bigger, wider wobble? | No vibrato at all | *A wide vibrato | A narrow vibrato | A quiet whisper
test: Which instrument can a player use to make vibrato? | A drum | A triangle | *A violin | A tambourine
test: Why do musicians use vibrato? | To make the note silent | To make the note shorter | *To make the sound warmer and richer | To stop the pitch changing
exam: Vibrato is a wobble in which of these? | the weight of a bag | *the pitch of a note | the colour of paint | the speed of a train
